{
  "description": "Distance bands (SPEC §10.1 / D-10, ARCH §12.2, API-NOTES §5.6). Single source of truth for web/src/core/geo.test.ts (Vitest) and GeoTests (XCTest, T-121): SPEC §10.7, AC-168, AC-352. Each case has an `fn` naming the function under test, a human `name`, its inputs and an `expect` object.",
  "conventions": [
    "Distances are metres; a key ending in Km is kilometres. Coordinates are decimal degrees.",
    "A non-finite number is written as the string \"NaN\", \"Infinity\" or \"-Infinity\" (JSON has no literal for them).",
    "haversine: expect.meters ± expect.tolM, and the same must hold with a and b swapped.",
    "band, pinBand: a case without thresholdsM uses defaultThresholdsM. Upper bounds are inclusive.",
    "thresholds: `raw` is the parsed RC `bands_m` value; anything that is not five finite, positive, strictly increasing numbers falls back to defaultThresholdsM. street, neighbourhood and district are locked to 250 / 1000 / 5000 because the band words name them (D-77): a table that changes one of them falls back. Only city and country are tunable. Extra keys are dropped.",
    "effective: e = max(haversine(pin, centre), radiusKm × 1000).",
    "pinBand: the hypothesis with the smallest e wins (ties keep the earlier one: the adversary's ranking, D-77); a hypothesis with a non-finite e is skipped; no usable hypothesis → band none with null hypothesisId and confidence.",
    "words: the copy ID and the SPEC §10.1 'Verdict words' verbatim. The words are the only distance text the UI shows: never metres (SR-07)."
  ],
  "earthRadiusM": 6371008.8,
  "defaultThresholdsM": {
    "street": 250,
    "neighbourhood": 1000,
    "district": 5000,
    "city": 30000,
    "country": 500000
  },
